By ten o'clock in the morning, the café got really busy.
That was my first big rush here.
People started standing in line.
In that rush, I could not make coffee.
For a beginner, it was very fast.
So Jessy quickly started making coffee.
I stood near the register.
I am learning to take out and give snacks to people.
A person bought a coffee and a piece of cake.
The total was one hundred and fifty rupees.
He gave me a five hundred rupee note.
I carefully counted the remaining amount.
I gave him three hundred and fifty rupees back.
During this time, Jessy gave his coffee.
The second person in the line wanted two coffees.
I gave them the bill very quickly.
I am learning to work like this with Jessy.
